    "summary": "Cotton woven indigo dyed skirt. Made of seven (7) narrow strips hand-woven and hand-sewn together selvedge to selvedge. The central strip is narrower than the others. The ends of the strips are finished with a hem. \r\n\r\nThe piece had been manually stitch-resist indigo dyed after weaving. It is decorated with bars and squares which together form six groups of warp-facing triangles. On the central strip is the inscription &quot;L&#039;enfant vos [vaut] mieux que l&#039;argent.&quot;",
